you want, AFAIK the books didn't delve too much into space beyond what you already noticed.<br /> <br /> Overall you seek a lot of hard answers where the setting is deliberately designed to offer none, leaving it up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T06:22:26-08:00","id":1556644,"title":"","content":"True! Though what I REALLY want is the headcanon of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T07:45:59-08:00","id":1556649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556639-void-spirits#post1556639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How far out into the depths of the Solar System do void spirits inhabit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, they probably want to stay away from the Solar System.<br /> <br /> <i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every </div> </div> </div></i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> planet in the Solar System has <i>mulhithim</i> (save for Earth, strangely enough). </div> </div> </div>I mean, the hypothetical existence of Gaia is a long standing question for the setting.<br /> <br /> However, I actually think it makes a certain sense. The Earth doesn't have the same 'purity' as the rest of the Solar System. The rest of the System don't have living beings spewing essence everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would there be <i>mulhithim</i> of dwarf planets in the outer edges of the Solar System, such as Pluto. </div> </div> </div>That seems the implication.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No <i>mulhithim</i> cone from foreign moons. Did Luna eat all her rivals? </div> </div> </div>That seems the obvious read. Maybe Luna is powerful enough to claim them all as her domain. If you somehow visit another moon in the system you just meet more Lunes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there void spirits from extrasolar space? </div> </div> </div>I took that as the implication.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do stars far away have spirit courts? </div> </div> </div>Seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would the Deep Shadow of a black hole be a mega-Wound? </div> </div> </div>I'd say no. Wounds are related to very human ideas of sin. A black hole is just a naturally occurring phenomena. <hr /><br /> <br /> In turn something occurs to me; Do the Border Marches start again at some point? I mean, Father Wolf was very powerful, but the universe is a vast place that should dwarf even the gods of the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T10:37:35-08:00","id":1556657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556639-void-spirits#post1556639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How far out into the depths of the Solar System do void spirits inhabit? <i>Every</i> planet in the Solar System has <i>mulhithim</i> (save for Earth, strangely enough). Would there be <i>mulhithim</i> of dwarf planets in the outer edges of the Solar System, such as Pluto.</div> </div> </div> </div>We see from Idigam Dread Power Call Void Spirit and the description from void leviathans they can come from farther away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No <i>mulhithim</i> cone from foreign moons. Did Luna eat all her rivals? </div> </div> </div>The implication I always got was that the situation on Earth is what is unnatural. In other planets, the planet spirit seems to be ruler of the local shadow. Whatever happened on Earth, they think it is unnatural that Luna is in charge. This is why they kill lunes, and the minions of lunes (Uratha). The rumor section suggests Luna is holding Gaia imprisoned. It might not be spot on but it might not be too far off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there void spirits from extrasolar space? Do stars far away have spirit courts? </div> </div> </div> It's where leviathans and other spirit come from so sure. It's probably understandable mulhithim are far less common, even keeping mind void spirits are rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would the Deep Shadow of a black hole be a mega-Wound? </div> </div> </div>I don't see why it would be it's not doing anything malicious.<br /> <br /> As monteparnas points out you might just read the section on void spirits in Shunned by the Moon, it's the extent of official information, all wrapped up in a brief write-up, aside from the Call Void Spirit power in the core. I'm sure Chris Allen has posted some about them on the forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556639-void-spirits?p=1556644#post1556644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though what I REALLY want is the headcanon of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I've caught onto this from your other posts, I can't speak for others but when it comes to headcanon I don't decide things setting wide. If I want something to work for a particular story, I'll have it be so for the story, but I wouldn't expect it to necessarily be canon in other stories I run.<br /> <br /> Why not share your own canon? If you're seeking brainstorming suggestions could be made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-15-2025, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T17:39:07-08:00","id":1556681,"title":"","content":"I think that once you open the can of the idea of there being spirits out far beyond human habitation you get really into the weeds of &quot;every existential implication of the fact that by all appearances we're a tiny spec in a vast indifferent and empty cosmos is actually alive and thinking&quot; comes to a point, and the Uratha and Shadow occultists who are able to devote time to thinking about it very much are left to desperately hoping that all of the spirits out there will overlook the Earth or that Luna can sufficiently keep them at bay, because if they're paying attention there's no getting around the fact that they outnumber you infinity to one.<br /> <br /> It's a funny implication to intimate for the fact that, all connotations of mythology aside, the patron of the Forsaken is an object hanging in space, and thus hovers on the boundary of making questions of astronomy sufficient to how the spirit world functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T18:26:40-08:00","id":1556684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556639-void-spirits?p=1556644#post1556644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True! Though what I REALLY want is the headcanon of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagined, but I'm unsure if this is the best approach to ask that.<br /> <br /> And as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">nofather</a> I don't think it really useful to have such answers even as headcanon. And I don't think this is an uncommon approach for CofD in particular, because this is first and foremost a mystery setting, where other themes are approached from mystery and informed by mystery. The modular approach also drives the point that nothing has to be true from one chronicle to another, especially since the very influential <i>Mirrors</i> book was published.<br /> <br /> Think about how in core Vampire each clan has a bunch of conflicting origin stories, or how sometimes books with setting write-ups (short or long) talk about the same place, but give quite distinct descriptions, or yet the sheer amount of things happening at those places that, even if you've read every single CofD book, still has no possible explanation and defies what we think we know about it.<br /> <br /> So, not knowing <b>is</b> the point, and even if a given ST wants a consistent answer across all their chronicles, they'll probably be better served with making them only when needed. Even because part of the point of this being a mystery setting is that we really don't have enough info to reach reasonable conclusions on any of this. Lore theories and headcanons are usually the result of piecing together what information we have and drawing lines that seem likely, or at least make some sense to the person. But CofD rarely gives many info, only more mysteries, we have little to work with.<br /> <br /> What else may be out there in space when even at our little blue rock reality seems inconsistent from place to place? Do you know Seattle doesn't have a Shadow, <b><u>but four</u></b>? And there's a big city in Turkey where natural portals to every Realm and alternate realities are everywhere, and all they take to use are keys based solely on movement. Anyone taking the right path, the right turn, or the wrong one as is more commonly the case, will end up somewhere else, and even some perfectly normal humans have learned how to use some for their advantage.<br /> <br /> Finally, I think for what you <i><b>really</b></i> want you should elaborate more on your questions. Short, direct questions will always seem to look for short, direct answers. Propose an actual exercise, give your own ideas, make a bunch of wild irreconcilable assumptions and ask what others want, anything at all. I'm naturally too verbose, but even I have problems engaging your approach with much beyond mirroring it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}